. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * We consider a model using two-stage least squares
. 
.         * As a good proxy of left-political preferences (hypothesis 2), we re
> verse plh0004, a variable associated to a self-reported
.         * political preferences. To do so, we reverse the scale where 10 is e
> xtreme left and 0 represents extreme right.
.         * Accordingly, we run a regression analysis where we instrument "havi
> ng at least one daughter" with a dummy equal to one if the first born was a d
> augher,
.         * and we use "leftpol" as dependent variable.
